  "title": "Artist of the Week: Marika Hackman",
  "content": "<div id=\"attachment_7115\" style=\"width: 970px\" class=\"wp-caption alignleft\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-7115\" class=\"size-full wp-image-7115\" src=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/04/hackman.jpg\" alt=\"Marika Hackman\" width=\"960\" height=\"638\" srcset=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/04/hackman.jpg 960w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/04/hackman-300x199.jpg 300w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/04/hackman-677x450.jpg 677w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/04/hackman-120x80.jpg 120w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\" /><p id=\"caption-attachment-7115\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Marika Hackman</p></div>\n<p class=\"ecxMsoNormal\"><b>Who is That?</b></p>\n<div class=\"ContentRightInner t_mbgc t_qtc t_urtc\">\n<div id=\"inboxControl0fv-ReadMessageContainer\" class=\"v-ReadMessageContainer slideOnResize\" tabindex=\"-1\">\n<div class=\"c-ReadMessage\" data-link=\"class{readMessageClass: ~tag.Show}\">\n<div id=\"ReadMessageScrollableSection\" class=\"rmMessages ClearBoth\" tabindex=\"-1\">\n<div id=\"readMessagePartControl247f\" class=\"c-ReadMessagePart ReadMsgContainer HasLayout ClearBoth HideShadows FullPart NoHistory Read RmIc\" data-link=\"class{:~tag.getHeaderCssClass(IsConversationPart, IsRead, IsDraft, IsTrustedSender, Items.length)}\">\n<div class=\"c-ReadMessagePartBody\" data-link=\"class{getClass:IsBodyExpanded}\">\n<div class=\"readMsgBody\">\n<div id=\"bodyreadMessagePartBodyControl252f\" class=\"ExternalClass MsgBodyContainer\" data-link=\"class{:~tag.cssClasses(PlainText, IsContentFiltered)}\">\n<div class=\"v-InboxFooterContainer\">\n<p class=\"ecxMsoNormal\">Marika Hackman is the former Burberry model-turned songstress, whose friendships with the likes of Cara Delevingne and Laura Marling have often been unfairly placed as points of interest ahead of her actual music.</p>\n<p class=\"ecxMsoNormal\"><b>What’s Her Sound?</b></p>\n<p class=\"ecxMsoNormal\">The folky pop of Laura Marling is indeed a good starting point, but Hackman&#8217;s music is full of dark edges, the songs always on the edge of slipping into an abyss, full of references to bones and skin and animalistic imagery. It also contains some touches of electronica, which juxtaposes nicely with the delicate and summery guitar work and brooding lyrical content &#8211; the song &#8216;Bath Is Black&#8217; being the perfect example of this.</p>\n<p class=\"ecxMsoNormal\"><b>What Is She Up To?</b></p>\n<p class=\"ecxMsoNormal\">Hackman recently released her debut album, <em>We Slept At Last</em>, which gained an excellent critical reception, and her new single, &#8216;Ophelia&#8217;, is released on 27 April. She is currently touring.</p>\n<p class=\"ecxMsoNormal\"><b>Where Can I See Her?</b></p>\n<p>Marika Hackman plays <a href=\"http://www.theklabristol.co.uk/live/458/marika-hackman\">Thekla on 9 April</a>.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p><iframe loading=\"lazy\" title=\"Marika Hackman - Animal Fear\" width=\"640\" height=\"360\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/AG4OIFLl394?feature=oembed\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe></p>\n<p><b>Conal Dougan</b></p>\n<p></p>",
